{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 4eccee225722015c57870448a0510202c3ced85b, tree edc354f8d476fccc7ef6a5fa1bd180fd6e56ec21, all 41 artifacts, for request 3a9c7da7 under my promise 7b1c7161. This head continues S6 (request 1c4557ec, promise 2de78527). The reporting artifact is the S6 implementation note. It answers the three points of planner direction e39770b5 and the two non-blocking points of my S6 verdict 0466f331.\n\n## What the delta changes\n\nThe head is one commit on the approved S6 head ed81b9d4. `git diff --name-only` against the gated source 77abe321 lists two paths: `notes/2026-11-01-git-read-token-after-revocation.md` and `notes/implementation/2026-11-21-s6-boundaries-and-custody.md`. The tree of this head is edc354f8, and `git merge-tree --write-tree d58ff62f 4eccee22` gives the same tree, so the head fast-forwards main. No source or test file changes. The passing S6 gate (END on 77abe321, exit 0, `cd27bd7b…`) therefore stands, and a notes-only head needs no new gate. The 41 artifacts filed at this head equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only d58ff62f 4eccee22`. `check-commit-messages` checks 7 commits and flags none, `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `git diff --check` is clean, and no added line names a local path.\n\n## The three points\n\n1. **The workspace token note.** The Status line now says that S6 adds local expiry for workspace token plaintext. The false sentence about `private_workspace_token` is replaced by a paragraph that matches the code at this head: `WorkspaceExpiry` indexes unread workspace and staging plaintext by the recorded `ends` time, the alarm clears due plaintext 64 rows at a time, and a legacy backfill indexes 64 rows at a time. The paragraph says that the token row and its ID stay for the existing provider revocation, which runs by ID, and that local expiry does not confirm provider revocation. I checked each claim: `#revoke` in `workspace-host.ts` calls `workspaceRevoke(repository, ask.id)`, and the cited ranges 